course: dictionary
lesson: 5811
title: Magma: hot melted rock under the Earth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. This is its context, and it leaves clues. «Melted rock is called magma while it is underground and lava once it pours out on the surface.» The clues are melted rock and underground, so magma must be hot melted rock that is still under the ground.
explain: «Magma rises because it is lighter than the solid rock around it.» Rises and lighter tell you that magma moves upwards through the solid rock. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try «melted rock» in place of magma and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Magma and lava are the same stuff in different places. Magma is underground; lava is the name once it reaches the surface. «A volcano erupts when magma rises into a chamber under the mountain.» Here the word is magma, because the melted rock has not yet come out.
fact: Magma is very hot melted rock under the Earth's surface.
fact: Magma is called lava once it pours out of a volcano onto the surface.
fact: Magma is lighter than the solid rock around it, so it rises.
fact: When magma cools slowly underground, it can form rock such as granite.
fact: A magma chamber is a space under a mountain where magma collects.
exercise: «Magma rises because it is lighter than the solid rock around it.» What does rises mean here? | It sinks down into the ground | It turns into water | *It moves upwards through the solid rock | It stays in one place forever
exercise: «Melted rock is called magma while it is underground.» What is magma? | A kind of gas that floats in the air | *Very hot melted rock | A tall mountain | A cold, hard stone
exercise: «Underground the melted rock is called magma; once it pours out on the surface it is called lava.» What is it called once it pours out? | Magma | Dust | *Lava | Steam
test: «A volcano erupts when magma, full of dissolved gas, rises into a chamber under the mountain.» What happens to the gas as magma nears the surface? | It disappears completely | *It comes out in bubbles, like fizzy drink when the cap comes off | It turns into solid rock | It stays still and stops moving
test: Which word means melted rock that has come out onto the surface? | Basalt | Granite | Magma | *Lava
exam: Magma that cools slowly underground forms which kind of rock? | Basalt | *Granite | Lava | Chalk
